  "summary": "blots@2.1.0 exfiltrates installer host identifiers to webhook.site on npm install",
  "details": "package.json declares preinstall and postinstall lifecycle scripts that invoke curl against a hardcoded webhook.site endpoint (https://webhook.site/d80b4602-8a87-4693-8510-6ff77c62788e), transmitting the installer's OS username (whoami), hostname, current working directory, and a unix timestamp as query parameters. This fires automatically on `npm install` without user interaction. The package ships no meaningful library content; its sole install-time effect is the identity/host reconnaissance beacon to a non-first-party destination.",
